Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: complete NPU receive frames once per poll batch

The NPU poll loop currently drains rx_skb and takes rx_lock for every
received frame. The ordinary DMA poll path completes a batch instead.
Keep NPU receive delivery bounded by the NAPI budget and drain the queued
frames once, before replenishing descriptors or completing NAPI. Flush
also when dequeue stops early, while leaving empty polls and the inactive
NPU path unchanged. Per-frame parsing, ordering and DMA ownership stay in
the existing receive callbacks.

--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -163,10 +163,11 @@
 			break;
 
 		dev->drv->rx_skb(dev, qid, skb, &info);
+		done++;
+	}
+
+	if (done)
 		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
-		done++;
-	}
-
 	mt76_npu_fill_rx_queue(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid]);
 out:
 	if (done < budget && napi_complete(napi))
